Transverse fetal thoracic image displays three parallel circular/oval echogenic outlines—pulmonary artery, ascending aorta, superior vena cava—coursing from left to right; variations include relative vessel size
Three vessel view ultrasound images show three parallel circular or oval echogenic lumens, the pulmonary artery, aorta, and superior vena cava, aligned across the upper chest with varying sizes, positions,
Axial fetal chest view displays three parallel circular/oval vessels across the upper mediastinum—leftmost largest, central slightly smaller, rightmost thinnest—Variation 8 shows increased spacing with mild caliber mismatch
In transverse fetal chest ultrasound the three-vessel view shows three tubular echoes—the pulmonary artery, ascending aorta and superior vena cava—varying in size, spacing and orientation, with occasional overlap,
In transverse fetal thoracic images the three-vessel view shows three parallel circular/oval vascular profiles—pulmonary artery leftmost, aorta central, superior vena cava rightmost—with variable relative sizes, spacing,
Three vessel view ultrasound shows three adjacent circular or ovoid echoes—pulmonary artery, aorta and superior vena cava—aligned in a V-shaped cluster with variable sizes, spacing, angulation and
The three-vessel view shows three round to oval echogenic tubular structures in the upper thorax—typically a largest leftmost, a medium central, and a small rightmost—with variation in size, spacing, angle, overlap, and echo intensity.
The three-vessel view shows three parallel circular or oval echoes—the largest left pulmonary artery, central ascending aorta, and smaller right superior vena cava—varying in relative size, spacing, alignment and branching;
Three vessel view ultrasound shows three circular to oval vascular profiles across the upper thorax arranged left to right, with color Doppler indicating differing flow and common variation in relative size, spacing, alignment.
Three-vessel-view ultrasound images show three circular or oval anechoic lumens with echogenic walls aligned side-by-side above the heart; Variation 6 often displays differing vessel diameters,
